/-!
# Gaussian Thompson sampling

Gaussian Thompson sampling with variance proxy `σ²` and a flat prior [LS, Theorem 36.3] is the
follow-the-perturbed-leader policy of [LS, Algorithm 24] whose perturbation of an arm `a` that has
been pulled `T_a > 0` times with empirical mean `μ̂_a` has law `𝒩(μ̂_a, σ² / T_a)`, and whose
perturbation of an arm that has not been pulled yet is `⊤`. The perturbations take values in
`EReal`, as the indices of index policies do: the policy pulls every arm once before comparing
Gaussian samples, and "pull each arm once" is the behaviour of the policy itself rather than a
separate initialization phase.

It is the limit of Thompson sampling with independent Gaussian priors on the means when the prior
variances tend to infinity. For `σ² ≠ 0` it is the instance of Thompson sampling for exponential
families `expFamilyTS` with the Gaussian family of variance `σ²` and its Jeffreys prior, a constant
multiple of Lebesgue measure on the natural parameter: the posterior of the natural parameter
`θ` of an arm pulled `s` times with sum of rewards `S` is `𝒩(S / (s σ²), 1 / (s σ²))` (for the
family generated by `𝒩(0, σ²)`), and its mean `σ² θ` has law `𝒩(S / s, σ² / s)`. It differs
from LML's `Bandits.tsAlgorithm`, which samples from the posterior of a prior over environments.

[LS] writes the variance `1 / t` of the update; the intended variance after `s` samples of the arm
is `1 / s`, here `σ² / s`.

## Main definitions

* `LMLExplore.Bandits.gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y`: the law of the perturbation of an arm that has
  been pulled `s` times with sum of rewards `y`: `δ_⊤` if `s = 0`, `𝒩(y / s, σ² / s)` otherwise.
* `LMLExplore.Bandits.gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a`: the law of the perturbation of arm `a` after the
  history `h` of length `n`: `δ_⊤` if `a` has not been pulled, `𝒩(μ̂_a, σ² / T_a)` otherwise.
* `LMLExplore.Bandits.gaussianTS σ2`: Gaussian Thompson sampling, the follow-the-perturbed-leader
  algorithm `perturbedLeaderAlgorithm` with perturbation laws `gaussianTSLaw σ2`.

## Main statements

* `gaussianTSStackLaw_eq_expFamilyTSStackLaw`, `gaussianTS_eq_expFamilyTS`: for `σ² ≠ 0`, the
  perturbation laws of Gaussian Thompson sampling are those of Thompson sampling for the Gaussian
  family of variance `σ²` with its Jeffreys prior, and the two algorithms are equal.
* `gaussianTSLaw_history`: along a sequence of rounds, the perturbation law in terms of LML's
  `pullCount` and `empMean`.
* `GaussianTS.pullCount_action_eq_zero`: along a run, while some arm has not been pulled, the arm
  played has not been pulled before.
* `GaussianTS.pullCount_card_eq_one`: Gaussian Thompson sampling pulls every arm exactly once
  during the first `Fintype.card α` rounds.
* `gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le_inv_of_add_sqrt_lt`: the perturbation of an arm pulled `s ≠ 0` times
  exceeds a level `c` with probability at most `1 / n` as soon as the UCB index
  `μ̂ + √(2 σ² log n / s)` of the arm is below `c`, by the Gaussian Chernoff bound.
* `sum_streamMeasure_inv_lt_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le`: [LS, Exercise 36.6(b)]: for a
  σ²-sub-Gaussian arm `i` of mean `μ_i < c`, the expected number of sample sizes `s < n` at which
  the perturbation of `i` exceeds `c` with probability more than `1 / n` is at most
  `1 + 2 σ² / (c - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)`, by [LS, Lemma 8.2].
* `hasLaw_sum_streamMeasure_of_eq_gaussianReal`: in the reward-stack model, the sum of the first `s`
  rewards of an arm with Gaussian rewards `𝒩(μ, σ²)` has law `𝒩(s μ, s σ²)`.
* `lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le`: for an arm with Gaussian rewards `𝒩(μ, σ²)`,
  `ε > 0` and `s ≠ 0` rewards, the probability `G_{j s}` that its perturbation exceeds `μ - ε`
  satisfies `E[1 / G_{j s} - 1] ≤ exp (-x / 4) / √2 + exp (-x / 2) (1 / √x + 1 / x)` with
  `x = s ε² / σ²`.
* `sum_lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le`: [LS, Exercise 36.6(a)]: for such an arm,
  `E[∑_{s < n} (1 / G_{j s} - 1)] ≤ σ² / ε² (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 σ² / ε²))`, uniformly in `n`.
* `GaussianTS.lintegral_pullCount_le`: [LS, Theorem 36.2] for Gaussian Thompson sampling, the
  bound on the expected number of pulls of an arm in terms of the perturbation laws of the
  reward-stack model.
* `GaussianTS.lintegral_pullCount_le_add_log`: [LS, Theorem 36.2] combined with
  [LS, Exercise 36.6(b)]: the bound on the expected number of pulls of a σ²-sub-Gaussian arm whose
  last term is logarithmic in the horizon.
* `GaussianTS.lintegral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit`: on a Gaussian bandit, both parts of
  [LS, Exercise 36.6] together: `E[T_i(n)] ≤ 2 + σ² / ε² (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 σ² / ε²))
  + 2 σ² / (μ_j - ε - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)` for arms with `μ_i < μ_j - ε`, and
  `GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit`, the same bound as a Bochner integral.
* `GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_le_mul_log_div_gap_sq_add`: on a Gaussian bandit, for a horizon
  `n ≥ 3` and an arm `a` whose gap `Δ_a` satisfies `8 σ² ≤ n Δ_a²`,
  `E[T_a(n)] ≤ 80 σ² log n / Δ_a² + 2`.
* `GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_eventually_le`: on a Gaussian bandit, for an arm `a` with positive
  gap `Δ_a` and every `c > 2 σ² / Δ_a²`, eventually `E[T_a(n)] ≤ c log n`.
* `gaussianTS_regret_eventually_le`: [LS, Theorem 36.3], upper bound of the asymptotic part: on a
  Gaussian bandit, for every `c > ∑_{a : Δ_a > 0} 2 σ² / Δ_a`, eventually `E[R_n] ≤ c log n`. The
  matching limit, through the Lai–Robbins lower bound, is
  `tendsto_gaussianTS_regret_div_log_gaussianBandit` in `LMLExplore.Bandits.AsymptoticOptimality`.
* `gaussianTS_regret_le_sqrt`: [LS, Theorem 36.3], minimax part: on a Gaussian bandit with `k`
  arms, `E[R_n] ≤ 18 √(σ² k n log n) + 2 ∑ a, Δ_a` at every horizon `n`.

## References

* [LS] T. Lattimore and Cs. Szepesvári, *Bandit Algorithms*, Cambridge University Press, 2020,
  Section 36.2, Theorem 36.3 and Exercise 36.6.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Learning Bandits

open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace LMLExplore.Bandits

section Law

variable {α : Type*} [DecidableEq α] {σ2 : ℝ≥0} {n : ℕ} {h : Hist Unit α ℝ n} {a : α}
  {s : ℕ} {y : ℝ}

/-- The law of the perturbation of an arm in Gaussian Thompson sampling, as a function of its
number of pulls `s` and its sum of rewards `y`: the Dirac mass at `⊤` if `s = 0`, and otherwise the
Gaussian law `𝒩(y / s, σ² / s)` on `EReal`. This is the perturbation law of the reward-stack model,
in which the sum of rewards after `s` pulls is the sum of the first `s` rewards of the stack. -/
noncomputable def gaussianTSStackLaw (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (s : ℕ) (y : ℝ) : Measure EReal :=
  if s = 0 then Measure.dirac ⊤ else (gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s)).map ((↑) : ℝ → EReal)

/-- The defining equation of `gaussianTSStackLaw`. -/
lemma gaussianTSStackLaw_def (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (s : ℕ) (y : ℝ) :
    gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y =
      if s = 0 then Measure.dirac ⊤ else (gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s)).map ((↑) : ℝ → EReal) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has not been pulled is `⊤`. -/
@[simp]
lemma gaussianTSStackLaw_zero (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (y : ℝ) : gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 0 y = Measure.dirac ⊤ := by
  simp [gaussianTSStackLaw_def]

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has been pulled `s ≠ 0` times with sum of rewards `y` has the
Gaussian law `𝒩(y / s, σ² / s)`. -/
@[simp]
lemma gaussianTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero (hs : s ≠ 0) :
    gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y = (gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s)).map ((↑) : ℝ → EReal) := by
  simp [gaussianTSStackLaw_def, hs]

instance : IsProbabilityMeasure (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y) := by
  rw [gaussianTSStackLaw_def]
  split_ifs <;> infer_instance

@[fun_prop]
lemma measurable_gaussianTSStackLaw (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (s : ℕ) :
    Measurable fun y : ℝ ↦ gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y := by
  by_cases hs : s = 0
  · simp [hs]
  · simp only [gaussianTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero hs]
    exact (Measure.measurable_map _ (by fun_prop)).comp
      (measurable_gaussianReal.comp ((measurable_id.div_const _).prodMk measurable_const))

/-- The law of the perturbation of arm `a` in Gaussian Thompson sampling at Lean round `n`, for the
history `h` of the first `n` rounds: the Dirac mass at `⊤` if the arm `a` has not been pulled, and
otherwise the Gaussian law `𝒩(μ̂_a, σ² / T_a)` on `EReal`, where `T_a` is the number of pulls of
`a` and `μ̂_a` its empirical mean. -/
noncomputable def gaussianTSLaw (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (n : ℕ) (h : Hist Unit α ℝ n) (a : α) :
    Measure EReal :=
  gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 (pullCount' n h a) (sumRewards' n h a)

/-- The defining equation of `gaussianTSLaw`: the law `gaussianTSStackLaw` at the number of pulls
and the sum of rewards of the arm. -/
lemma gaussianTSLaw_def (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (n : ℕ) (h : Hist Unit α ℝ n) (a : α) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a = gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 (pullCount' n h a) (sumRewards' n h a) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has not been pulled is `⊤`. -/
@[simp]
lemma gaussianTSLaw_of_pullCount'_eq_zero (h0 : pullCount' n h a = 0) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a = Measure.dirac ⊤ := by
  simp [gaussianTSLaw_def, h0]

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has been pulled has the Gaussian law `𝒩(μ̂_a, σ² / T_a)`. -/
lemma gaussianTSLaw_of_pullCount'_ne_zero (h0 : pullCount' n h a ≠ 0) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a =
      (gaussianReal (empMean' n h a) (σ2 / pullCount' n h a)).map ((↑) : ℝ → EReal) := by
  simp [gaussianTSLaw_def, h0, empMean']

instance : IsProbabilityMeasure (gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a) := by
  rw [gaussianTSLaw_def]
  infer_instance

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has been pulled is almost surely finite. -/
lemma gaussianTSLaw_Ici_top_eq_zero (h0 : pullCount' n h a ≠ 0) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a (Set.Ici ⊤) = 0 := by
  have h_empty : ((↑) : ℝ → EReal) ⁻¹' Set.Ici ⊤ = ∅ := by ext; simp
  rw [gaussianTSLaw_of_pullCount'_ne_zero h0,
    Measure.map_apply (by fun_prop) measurableSet_Ici, h_empty, measure_empty]

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has not been pulled is `⊤`, almost surely not below `⊤`. -/
lemma gaussianTSLaw_Iio_top_eq_zero (h0 : pullCount' n h a = 0) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a (Set.Iio ⊤) = 0 := by
  simp [h0]

@[fun_prop]
lemma measurable_gaussianTSLaw [MeasurableSpace α] [MeasurableSingletonClass α] (σ2 : ℝ≥0)
    (n : ℕ) (a : α) : Measurable fun h : Hist Unit α ℝ n ↦ gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a :=
  (measurable_from_prod_countable_right (f := fun q : ℕ × ℝ ↦ gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 q.1 q.2)
    (measurable_gaussianTSStackLaw σ2)).comp
    ((measurable_pullCount' n a).prodMk (measurable_sumRewards' n a))

/-- Along a sequence of rounds `(O, A, R)`, the perturbation law of an arm at round `n` is the
Dirac mass at `⊤` if the arm has not been pulled before `n`, and otherwise `𝒩(μ̂_a, σ² / T_a)` for
the number of pulls `T_a = pullCount A a n ω` and the empirical mean `μ̂_a = empMean A R a n ω`. -/
lemma gaussianTSLaw_history {Ω : Type*} (O : ℕ → Ω → Unit) (A : ℕ → Ω → α) (R : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (σ2 : ℝ≥0) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) (a : α) :
    gaussianTSLaw σ2 n (history O A R n ω) a = if pullCount A a n ω = 0 then Measure.dirac ⊤ else
      (gaussianReal (empMean A R a n ω) (σ2 / pullCount A a n ω)).map ((↑) : ℝ → EReal) := by
  rw [gaussianTSLaw_def, gaussianTSStackLaw_def, ← pullCount_eq_pullCount',
    ← sumRewards_eq_sumRewards', empMean]

end Law

section Concentration

variable {σ2 : ℝ≥0} {s : ℕ} {y : ℝ}

/-- The perturbation of an arm that has been pulled `s ≠ 0` times with sum of rewards `y` exceeds a
level `c` with probability at most `1 / n` as soon as the index `y / s + √(2 σ² log n / s)` of
[LS, Algorithm 6] is below `c`, here in the form `y + √(2 σ² log n s) < s c`. This is the Gaussian
Chernoff bound `P(𝒩(m, σ² / s) > c) ≤ exp (-s (c - m)² / (2 σ²))` for `m = y / s < c`. -/
lemma gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le_inv_of_add_sqrt_lt {c : ℝ} (n : ℕ) (hs : s ≠ 0)
    (h : y + √(2 * σ2 * Real.log n * s) < s * c) :
    gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y (Set.Ioi (c : EReal)) ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ := by
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hn
  · simp
  have hs' : (0 : ℝ) < s := by positivity
  have hsqrt := Real.sqrt_nonneg (2 * σ2 * Real.log n * s)
  have hmc : y / s < c := by
    rw [div_lt_iff₀ hs']
    linarith
  rw [gaussianTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero hs, Measure.map_apply (by fun_prop) measurableSet_Ioi,
    EReal.preimage_coe_Ioi]
  rcases eq_or_ne σ2 0 with rfl | hσ
  · -- with zero variance, the perturbation is the empirical mean, which is below `c`
    simp [Set.mem_Ioi, hmc.le]
  -- with `d = s c - y`, the hypothesis says `2 σ² log n s < d²`
  have hd : 2 * σ2 * Real.log n * s < (s * c - y) ^ 2 :=
    (Real.sqrt_lt' (by linarith)).mp (by linarith)
  have hexp :
      Real.exp (-(c - y / s) ^ 2 / (2 * ((σ2 / s : ℝ≥0) : ℝ))) ≤ Real.exp (-Real.log n) := by
    gcongr
    have hσ' : (0 : ℝ) < σ2 := by positivity
    rw [NNReal.coe_div, NNReal.coe_natCast, div_le_iff₀ (by positivity)]
    field_simp
    nlinarith
  calc gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s) (Set.Ioi c)
      ≤ gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s) (Set.Ici c) := measure_mono Set.Ioi_subset_Ici_self
    _ = ENNReal.ofReal ((gaussianReal (y / s) (σ2 / s)).real (Set.Ici c)) :=
        (ofReal_measureReal).symm
    _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-Real.log n)) :=
        ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal ((measureReal_Ici_gaussianReal_le_exp _ hmc.le).trans hexp)
    _ = (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ := by
        rw [Real.exp_neg, Real.exp_log (by positivity), ENNReal.ofReal_inv_of_pos (by positivity),
          ENNReal.ofReal_natCast]

/-- **[LS, Exercise 36.6(b)].** Let arm `i` be σ²-sub-Gaussian with mean `μ_i` and let `c > μ_i`.
In the reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν`, write `G_{i s}` for the probability that the
perturbation of Gaussian Thompson sampling of `i` after its first `s` rewards exceeds `c`. Then the
expected number of sample sizes `s < n` with `G_{i s} > 1 / n` is at most
`1 + 2 σ² / (c - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)`, which is `2 σ² log n / (c - μ_i)² + o(log n)`.

[LS] takes `c = μ* - ε` for the mean `μ*` of an optimal arm. -/
theorem sum_streamMeasure_inv_lt_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]
    {ν : Kernel α ℝ} [IsMarkovKernel ν] {i : α}
    (hν : HasSubgaussianMGF (fun x ↦ x - (ν i)[id]) σ2 (ν i)) {c : ℝ} (hc : (ν i)[id] < c)
    (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, streamMeasure ν {x | (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ <
        gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k i) (Set.Ioi (c : EReal))} ≤
      ENNReal.ofReal (1 + 2 * σ2 / (c - (ν i)[id]) ^ 2 *
        (Real.log n + √(Real.pi * Real.log n) + 1)) := by
  -- the event `G_{i s} > 1 / n` forces the index of [LS, Algorithm 6] at exploration level
  -- `log n` to be at least `c`, whose expected count is bounded by [LS, Lemma 8.2]
  refine le_trans ?_ (ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal (sum_measureReal_streamMeasure_mul_le_sum_add_sqrt_le
    hν (sub_pos.2 hc) (Real.log_natCast_nonneg n) n))
  rw [ENNReal.ofReal_sum_of_nonneg fun _ _ ↦ measureReal_nonneg]
  refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun s _ ↦ ?_
  rw [ofReal_measureReal]
  refine measure_mono fun x hx ↦ ?_
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, add_sub_cancel] at hx ⊢
  rcases eq_or_ne s 0 with rfl | hs
  · simp
  by_contra hlt
  exact (gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le_inv_of_add_sqrt_lt n hs (not_le.mp hlt)).not_gt hx

/-- In the reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν`, if arm `j` has Gaussian rewards `𝒩(μ, σ²)`, the sum
of its first `s` rewards has law `𝒩(s μ, s σ²)`. -/
lemma hasLaw_sum_streamMeasure_of_eq_gaussianReal {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]
    {ν : Kernel α ℝ} [IsMarkovKernel ν] {j : α} {μ : ℝ} (hν : ν j = gaussianReal μ σ2) (s : ℕ) :
    HasLaw (fun x : ℕ → α → ℝ ↦ ∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j) (gaussianReal (s * μ) (s * σ2))
      (streamMeasure ν) := by
  simpa using (iIndepFun_eval_streamMeasure'' ν j).hasLaw_sum_gaussianReal
    (m := fun _ ↦ μ) (v := fun _ ↦ σ2) (fun k ↦ hν ▸ hasLaw_eval_eval_streamMeasure ν k j)
    (Finset.range s)

/-- Let arm `j` have Gaussian rewards `𝒩(μ, σ²)` with `σ² ≠ 0`, let `ε > 0` and `s ≠ 0`. In the
reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν`, write `G_{j s}` for the probability that the perturbation of
Gaussian Thompson sampling of `j` after its first `s` rewards exceeds `μ - ε`. Then, with
`x = s ε² / σ²`, `E[1 / G_{j s} - 1] ≤ exp (-x / 4) / √2 + exp (-x / 2) (1 / √x + 1 / x)`.

The perturbation exceeds `μ - ε` with probability `P(Z > U)` for a standard Gaussian `Z`, where
`U ∼ 𝒩(-√x, 1)` is the standardized gap between `μ - ε` and the empirical mean, so this is
`lintegral_inv_gaussianReal_Ioi_sub_one_le`. -/
theorem lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]
    {ν : Kernel α ℝ} [IsMarkovKernel ν] {j : α} {μ : ℝ} (hν : ν j = gaussianReal μ σ2)
    (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hs : s ≠ 0) :
    ∫⁻ x, (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j)
        (Set.Ioi ((μ - ε : ℝ) : EReal)))⁻¹ - 1 ∂(streamMeasure ν) ≤
      ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-(s * ε ^ 2 / σ2) / 4) / √2 + Real.exp (-(s * ε ^ 2 / σ2) / 2) *
        (1 / √(s * ε ^ 2 / σ2) + 1 / (s * ε ^ 2 / σ2))) := by
  have hv : σ2 / (s : ℝ≥0) ≠ 0 := by positivity
  -- the standard deviation `τ` of the perturbation and the standardized gap `a = ε / τ`
  set τ := √((σ2 / (s : ℝ≥0) : ℝ≥0) : ℝ) with hτ
  have hτ0 : 0 < τ := by positivity
  set a := ε / τ with ha
  have ha0 : 0 < a := by positivity
  have hτ2 : τ ^ 2 = σ2 / s := by
    rw [hτ, Real.sq_sqrt (by positivity), NNReal.coe_div, NNReal.coe_natCast]
  have ha2 : a ^ 2 = s * ε ^ 2 / σ2 := by
    rw [ha, div_pow, hτ2]
    field_simp
  -- `G_{j s}` is the standard Gaussian tail at the standardized gap
  have hG (y : ℝ) : gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y (Set.Ioi ((μ - ε : ℝ) : EReal)) =
      gaussianReal 0 1 (Set.Ioi ((μ - ε - y / s) / τ)) := by
    rw [gaussianTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero hs, Measure.map_apply (by fun_prop) measurableSet_Ioi,
      EReal.preimage_coe_Ioi, ← ofReal_measureReal, ← ofReal_measureReal,
      TauCeti.Probability.measureReal_Ioi_gaussianReal_eq_cdf _ hv,
      TauCeti.Probability.measureReal_Ioi_gaussianReal_eq_cdf 0 one_ne_zero]
    congr 2
    simp only [NNReal.coe_one, Real.sqrt_one, div_one, zero_sub, ← neg_div, neg_sub, hτ]
  -- the standardized gap has law `𝒩(-a, 1)` under the stream model
  have hT : HasLaw (fun x : ℕ → α → ℝ ↦ (μ - ε - (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j) / s) / τ)
      (gaussianReal (-a) 1) (streamMeasure ν) := by
    have h := gaussianReal_add_const (gaussianReal_mul_const
      (hasLaw_sum_streamMeasure_of_eq_gaussianReal hν s) (-(1 / (s * τ)))) ((μ - ε) / τ)
    convert h using 2
    · field_simp
      ring
    · rw [ha]
      field_simp
      ring
    · ext
      simp only [NNReal.coe_mul, NNReal.coe_mk, NNReal.coe_natCast, NNReal.coe_one]
      rw [neg_sq, div_pow, mul_pow, hτ2]
      field_simp
  have hmeas : Measurable fun u : ℝ ↦ (gaussianReal 0 1 (Set.Ioi u))⁻¹ - 1 := by
    have : Antitone fun u : ℝ ↦ gaussianReal 0 1 (Set.Ioi u) := fun _ _ h ↦
      measure_mono (Set.Ioi_subset_Ioi h)
    exact this.measurable.inv.sub_const 1
  simp_rw [hG]
  rw [hT.lintegral_comp hmeas.aemeasurable]
  refine (lintegral_inv_gaussianReal_Ioi_sub_one_le ha0).trans_eq ?_
  rw [← ha2, Real.sqrt_sq ha0.le]

/-- The sum over the sample sizes of the bounds of
`lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le`: for `κ > 0` and `x = (s + 1) κ`,
`∑_{s < n} (exp (-x / 4) / √2 + exp (-x / 2) (1 / √x + 1 / x)) ≤ (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 / κ)) / κ`. -/
private lemma sum_range_exp_div_sqrt_two_add_le {κ : ℝ} (hκ : 0 < κ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, (Real.exp (-((s + 1) * κ) / 4) / √2 + Real.exp (-((s + 1) * κ) / 2) *
      (1 / √((s + 1) * κ) + 1 / ((s + 1) * κ))) ≤ (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 / κ)) / κ := by
  -- each term is at most `2 exp (-x / 4) + 2 exp (-x / 2) / x`
  have hterm (s : ℕ) : Real.exp (-((s + 1) * κ) / 4) / √2 + Real.exp (-((s + 1) * κ) / 2) *
      (1 / √((s + 1) * κ) + 1 / ((s + 1) * κ)) ≤
      2 * Real.exp (-(κ / 4 * (s + 1))) +
        2 / κ * (Real.exp (-(κ / 2 * (s + 1))) / (s + 1)) := by
    set x := (s + 1 : ℝ) * κ with hx
    have hx0 : 0 < x := by positivity
    have h1 : Real.exp (-x / 4) / √2 ≤ Real.exp (-x / 4) :=
      div_le_self (Real.exp_pos _).le (Real.one_le_sqrt.2 one_le_two)
    have h2 : Real.exp (-x / 2) ≤ Real.exp (-x / 4) := Real.exp_le_exp.2 (by linarith)
    have h3 : 1 / √x ≤ 1 + 1 / x := by
      rcases le_total 1 x with h | h
      · have : 1 / √x ≤ 1 := by
          rw [div_le_one (by positivity)]
          exact Real.one_le_sqrt.2 h
        linarith [show 0 ≤ 1 / x by positivity]
      · have hxs : x ≤ √x := (Real.le_sqrt hx0.le hx0.le).2 (by nlinarith)
        have : 1 / √x ≤ 1 / x := one_div_le_one_div_of_le hx0 hxs
        linarith
    have h4 : Real.exp (-x / 2) * (2 / x) =
        2 / κ * (Real.exp (-(κ / 2 * (s + 1))) / (s + 1)) := by
      rw [hx]
      field_simp
    have h5 : Real.exp (-x / 4) = Real.exp (-(κ / 4 * (s + 1))) := by
      rw [hx]
      ring_nf
    calc Real.exp (-x / 4) / √2 + Real.exp (-x / 2) * (1 / √x + 1 / x)
        ≤ Real.exp (-x / 4) + Real.exp (-x / 2) * (1 + 1 / x + 1 / x) := by gcongr
      _ = Real.exp (-x / 4) + Real.exp (-x / 2) + Real.exp (-x / 2) * (2 / x) := by ring
      _ ≤ 2 * Real.exp (-(κ / 4 * (s + 1))) +
          2 / κ * (Real.exp (-(κ / 2 * (s + 1))) / (s + 1)) := by
        rw [h4, ← h5]
        linarith
  refine (Finset.sum_le_sum fun s _ ↦ hterm s).trans ?_
  rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.mul_sum]
  have h1 := Real.sum_range_exp_neg_mul_le (c := κ / 4) (by positivity) n
  have h2 := Real.sum_range_exp_neg_mul_div_le (c := κ / 2) (by positivity) n
  rw [one_div_div] at h2
  calc 2 * ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, Real.exp (-(κ / 4 * (s + 1))) +
        2 / κ * ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, Real.exp (-(κ / 2 * (s + 1))) / (s + 1)
      ≤ 2 * (κ / 4)⁻¹ + 2 / κ * Real.log (1 + 2 / κ) := by gcongr
    _ = (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 / κ)) / κ := by
        field_simp
        ring

/-- **[LS, Exercise 36.6(a)].** Let arm `j` have Gaussian rewards `𝒩(μ, σ²)` with `σ² ≠ 0`, and
let `ε > 0`. In the reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν`, write `G_{j s}` for the probability that
the perturbation of Gaussian Thompson sampling of `j` after its first `s` rewards exceeds
`μ - ε`. Then, uniformly in the horizon `n`,
`E[∑_{s < n} (1 / G_{j s} - 1)] ≤ σ² / ε² (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 σ² / ε²))`.

This is the first sum in the bound of [LS, Theorem 36.2] (`GaussianTS.lintegral_pullCount_le`)
for an optimal arm `j`; [LS] states it as `O(log (1 / ε) / ε²)` for `σ² = 1`. -/
theorem sum_lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]
    {ν : Kernel α ℝ} [IsMarkovKernel ν] {j : α} {μ : ℝ} (hν : ν j = gaussianReal μ σ2)
    (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, ∫⁻ x, (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j)
        (Set.Ioi ((μ - ε : ℝ) : EReal)))⁻¹ - 1 ∂(streamMeasure ν) ≤
      ENNReal.ofReal (σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2))) := by
  set I : ℕ → ℝ≥0∞ := fun s ↦ ∫⁻ x, (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j)
    (Set.Ioi ((μ - ε : ℝ) : EReal)))⁻¹ - 1 ∂(streamMeasure ν) with hI
  -- before the first pull, the perturbation is `⊤` and `G_{j 0} = 1`
  have hI0 : I 0 = 0 := by
    have h_top : (⊤ : EReal) ∈ Set.Ioi ((μ - ε : ℝ) : EReal) := EReal.coe_lt_top _
    simp only [hI, Finset.range_zero, Finset.sum_empty, gaussianTSStackLaw_zero,
      Measure.dirac_apply_of_mem h_top]
    simp
  have hκ : 0 < ε ^ 2 / σ2 := by positivity
  have hsucc (s : ℕ) : I (s + 1) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 4) / √2 +
      Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 2) *
        (1 / √((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) + 1 / ((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)))) := by
    have h := lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le hν hσ hε s.succ_ne_zero
    rw [Nat.cast_succ, mul_div_assoc] at h
    exact h
  calc ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, I s ≤ ∑ s ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), I s :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset (Finset.range_subset_range.2 n.le_succ)
    _ = ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, I (s + 1) := by rw [Finset.sum_range_succ', hI0, add_zero]
    _ ≤ ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 4) / √2 +
          Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 2) *
            (1 / √((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) + 1 / ((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)))) :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun s _ ↦ hsucc s
    _ = ENNReal.ofReal (∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, (Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 4) / √2 +
          Real.exp (-((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) / 2) *
            (1 / √((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2)) + 1 / ((s + 1) * (ε ^ 2 / σ2))))) :=
        (ENNReal.ofReal_sum_of_nonneg fun _ _ ↦ by positivity).symm
    _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2))) := by
        refine ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal ((sum_range_exp_div_sqrt_two_add_le hκ n).trans_eq ?_)
        rw [div_div_eq_mul_div, div_div_eq_mul_div]
        ring

end Concentration

section Algorithm

variable {α : Type*} [Fintype α] [Nonempty α] [DecidableEq α] [MeasurableSpace α]
  [MeasurableSingletonClass α]

/-- Gaussian Thompson sampling with variance proxy `σ²` and a flat prior [LS, Theorem 36.3]: the
follow-the-perturbed-leader algorithm that samples, at round `n`, independent perturbations of laws
`gaussianTSLaw σ2 n h a` and plays an arm of maximal perturbation, ties being broken by LML's
`argmax`. -/
noncomputable def gaussianTS (σ2 : ℝ≥0) : Algorithm Unit α ℝ :=
  perturbedLeaderAlgorithm (fun n x a ↦ gaussianTSLaw σ2 n x.1 a)
    (fun n a ↦ (measurable_gaussianTSLaw σ2 n a).comp measurable_fst) fun _ _ _ ↦ inferInstance

/-- Gaussian Thompson sampling is the follow-the-perturbed-leader algorithm with perturbation laws
`gaussianTSLaw σ2`. -/
lemma gaussianTS_def (σ2 : ℝ≥0) :
    gaussianTS (α := α) σ2 =
      perturbedLeaderAlgorithm (fun n x a ↦ gaussianTSLaw σ2 n x.1 a)
        (fun n a ↦ (measurable_gaussianTSLaw σ2 n a).comp measurable_fst)
        fun _ _ _ ↦ inferInstance :=
  (rfl)

/-- For `σ² ≠ 0`, the perturbation law of Gaussian Thompson sampling of an arm pulled `s` times
with sum of rewards `y` is that of Thompson sampling for the Gaussian family of variance `σ²`,
generated by any `𝒩(m, σ²)`, with its Jeffreys prior. -/
theorem gaussianTSStackLaw_eq_expFamilyTSStackLaw (m : ℝ) {σ2 : ℝ≥0} (hσ2 : σ2 ≠ 0) (s : ℕ)
    (y : ℝ) :
    gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s y =
      expFamilyTSStackLaw (gaussianReal m σ2) ((gaussianReal m σ2).jeffreysPrior id) s y := by
  rcases eq_or_ne s 0 with rfl | hs
  · simp
  have hpost := expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior m hσ2 hs y
  rw [gaussianTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero hs,
    expFamilyTSStackLaw_of_ne_zero hs (by rw [hpost]; exact IsProbabilityMeasure.ne_zero _),
    ← map_deriv_cgf_expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior m hσ2 hs,
    Measure.map_map (by fun_prop) (measurable_deriv _), Function.comp_def]

/-- For `σ² ≠ 0`, Gaussian Thompson sampling is Thompson sampling for exponential families with the
Gaussian family of variance `σ²` on every arm, generated by any `𝒩(m a, σ²)`, and its Jeffreys
prior. -/
theorem gaussianTS_eq_expFamilyTS (m : α → ℝ) {σ2 : ℝ≥0} (hσ2 : σ2 ≠ 0) :
    gaussianTS σ2 = expFamilyTS (fun a ↦ gaussianReal (m a) σ2)
      (fun a ↦ (gaussianReal (m a) σ2).jeffreysPrior id) := by
  rw [gaussianTS_def, expFamilyTS_def]
  congr with n x a
  rw [gaussianTSLaw_def, expFamilyTSLaw_def, gaussianTSStackLaw_eq_expFamilyTSStackLaw (m a) hσ2]

namespace GaussianTS

variable {σ2 : ℝ≥0} {Ω : Type*} {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {env : Environment Unit α ℝ}
  {P : Measure Ω} [IsFiniteMeasure P] {O : ℕ → Ω → Unit} {A : ℕ → Ω → α} {R : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}

/-- Along a run of Gaussian Thompson sampling, while some arm has not been pulled yet, the arm
played has not been pulled before. -/
lemma pullCount_action_eq_zero (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) env P) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ n, (∃ b, pullCount A b n ω = 0) → pullCount A (A n ω) n ω = 0 := by
  -- arms that have not been pulled have perturbation `⊤` and the others almost surely have a
  -- finite perturbation
  rw [ae_all_iff]
  intro n
  rw [gaussianTS_def] at h
  have hpc (b : α) : Measurable fun x : Hist Unit α ℝ n × Unit ↦ pullCount' n x.1 b :=
    (measurable_pullCount' n b).comp measurable_fst
  -- the set of pasts at which `a` has been pulled while some arm has not
  let s (a : α) : Set (Hist Unit α ℝ n × Unit) :=
    {x | pullCount' n x.1 a = 0}ᶜ ∩ ⋃ b, {x | pullCount' n x.1 b = 0}
  have hs (a : α) : MeasurableSet (s a) :=
    ((hpc a) (measurableSet_singleton 0)).compl.inter
      (MeasurableSet.iUnion fun b ↦ (hpc b) (measurableSet_singleton 0))
  have hnull (a : α) :
      P ((fun ω ↦ (history O A R n ω, O n ω)) ⁻¹' s a ∩ A n ⁻¹' {a}) = 0 := by
    refine PerturbedLeader.measure_preimage_inter_action_eq_zero h n (hs a) a fun x hx ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨hxa, hxb⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp hxb
    exact ⟨b, ⊤, gaussianTSLaw_Ici_top_eq_zero hxa,
      gaussianTSLaw_Iio_top_eq_zero hb⟩
  have hsub : {ω | ¬((∃ b, pullCount A b n ω = 0) → pullCount A (A n ω) n ω = 0)} ⊆
      ⋃ a, (fun ω ↦ (history O A R n ω, O n ω)) ⁻¹' s a ∩ A n ⁻¹' {a} := by
    intro ω hω
    simp only [Classical.not_imp, Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hω
    obtain ⟨⟨b, hb⟩, hne⟩ := hω
    rw [pullCount_eq_pullCount' (O := O) (R' := R)] at hb hne
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨A n ω, ⟨hne, Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨b, hb⟩⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [ae_iff]
  exact measure_mono_null hsub (measure_iUnion_null hnull)

/-- Gaussian Thompson sampling pulls every arm exactly once during the first `Fintype.card α`
rounds. -/
lemma pullCount_card_eq_one (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) env P) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ a, pullCount A a (Fintype.card α) ω = 1 := by
  filter_upwards [pullCount_action_eq_zero h] with ω hω a
  exact pullCount_card_eq_one_of_forall_pullCount_action_eq_zero
    (fun n hn ↦ hω n (exists_pullCount_eq_zero_of_lt_card hn)) a

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.2] for Gaussian Thompson sampling.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson sampling
against the stochastic bandit `Environment.bandit ν`, for arms `i ≠ j`, a level `c` and a horizon
`n`, `E[T_i(n)] ≤ 1 + E[∑_{s < n} (G_{j s}⁻¹ - 1)] + ∑_{s < n} P(G_{i s} > 1 / n)`, where in the
reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν`, `G_{a s}` is the probability that the perturbation of arm `a`
after `s` pulls exceeds `c`: the probability that a sample of `𝒩(μ̂_{a s}, σ² / s)` exceeds `c`,
for the mean `μ̂_{a s}` of the first `s` rewards of `a`, and `G_{a 0} = 1` if `c < ⊤`. -/
theorem lintegral_pullCount_le [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {ν : Kernel α ℝ} [IsMarkovKernel ν]
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit ν) P) {i j : α} (hij : i ≠ j)
    (c : EReal) (n : ℕ) :
    ∫⁻ ω, (pullCount A i n ω : ℝ≥0∞) ∂P ≤
      1 + ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, ∫⁻ x,
          (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j) (Set.Ioi c))⁻¹ - 1
            ∂(streamMeasure ν) +
        ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, streamMeasure ν {x | (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ <
          gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k i) (Set.Ioi c)} :=
  -- the perturbation law of an arm is a function of its number of pulls and its sum of rewards
  PerturbedLeader.lintegral_pullCount_le h (fun _ ↦ gaussianTSStackLaw σ2)
    (fun _ ↦ measurable_gaussianTSStackLaw σ2) (fun t x a ↦ gaussianTSLaw_def σ2 t x.1 a) hij c n

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.2] with [LS, Exercise 36.6(b)] for Gaussian Thompson sampling.** In a run of
Gaussian Thompson sampling against the stochastic bandit `Environment.bandit ν`, let `i ≠ j` be
arms, `i` σ²-sub-Gaussian with mean `μ_i`, and `c > μ_i` a level. Then for every horizon `n`,
`E[T_i(n)] ≤ 1 + E[∑_{s < n} (G_{j s}⁻¹ - 1)] + 1 + 2 σ² / (c - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)`,
where `G_{j s}` is the probability that the perturbation of arm `j` after its first `s` rewards in
the reward-stack model `streamMeasure ν` exceeds `c`. -/
theorem lintegral_pullCount_le_add_log [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {ν : Kernel α ℝ}
    [IsMarkovKernel ν] (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit ν) P) {i j : α}
    (hij : i ≠ j) (hν : HasSubgaussianMGF (fun x ↦ x - (ν i)[id]) σ2 (ν i)) {c : ℝ}
    (hc : (ν i)[id] < c) (n : ℕ) :
    ∫⁻ ω, (pullCount A i n ω : ℝ≥0∞) ∂P ≤
      1 + ∑ s ∈ Finset.range n, ∫⁻ x,
          (gaussianTSStackLaw σ2 s (∑ k ∈ Finset.range s, x k j) (Set.Ioi (c : EReal)))⁻¹ - 1
            ∂(streamMeasure ν) +
        ENNReal.ofReal (1 + 2 * σ2 / (c - (ν i)[id]) ^ 2 *
          (Real.log n + √(Real.pi * Real.log n) + 1)) :=
  (lintegral_pullCount_le h hij c n).trans
    (add_le_add le_rfl (sum_streamMeasure_inv_lt_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_le hν hc n))

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.2] with [LS, Exercise 36.6] for Gaussian Thompson sampling on a Gaussian
bandit.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson sampling with variance proxy `σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian
bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2`, let `ε > 0` and let `i`, `j` be arms with `μ_i < μ_j - ε`. Then for
every horizon `n`,
`E[T_i(n)] ≤ 1 + σ² / ε² (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 σ² / ε²))
  + 1 + 2 σ² / (μ_j - ε - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)`.

For an optimal arm `j` the gap `μ_j - μ_i` is `Δ_i`, so `E[T_i(n)]` is at most
`2 σ² log n / (Δ_i - ε)² + o(log n)`, the bound that [LS, Theorem 36.3] sums over the
suboptimal arms. -/
theorem lintegral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {μ : α → ℝ}
    (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P)
    {i j : α} {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hij : μ i < μ j - ε) (n : ℕ) :
    ∫⁻ ω, (pullCount A i n ω : ℝ≥0∞) ∂P ≤
      1 + ENNReal.ofReal (σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2))) +
        ENNReal.ofReal (1 + 2 * σ2 / (μ j - ε - μ i) ^ 2 *
          (Real.log n + √(Real.pi * Real.log n) + 1)) := by
  have hne : i ≠ j := by
    rintro rfl
    linarith
  have h_le := lintegral_pullCount_le_add_log h hne (hasSubgaussianMGF_gaussianBandit μ σ2 i)
    (c := μ j - ε) (by rwa [integral_id_gaussianBandit]) n
  rw [integral_id_gaussianBandit] at h_le
  refine h_le.trans ?_
  gcongr
  exact sum_lintegral_inv_gaussianTSStackLaw_Ioi_sub_one_le (gaussianBandit_apply μ σ2 j) hσ hε n

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.2] with [LS, Exercise 36.6] for Gaussian Thompson sampling on a Gaussian
bandit**, as a Bochner integral. In a run of Gaussian Thompson sampling with variance proxy
`σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2`, let `ε > 0` and let `i`, `j` be arms
with `μ_i < μ_j - ε`. Then for every horizon `n`,
`E[T_i(n)] ≤ 2 + σ² / ε² (8 + 2 log (1 + 2 σ² / ε²))
  + 2 σ² / (μ_j - ε - μ_i)² (log n + √(π log n) + 1)`. -/
theorem integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {μ : α → ℝ}
    (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P)
    {i j : α} {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hij : μ i < μ j - ε) (n : ℕ) :
    P[fun ω ↦ (pullCount A i n ω : ℝ)] ≤
      2 + σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2)) +
        2 * σ2 / (μ j - ε - μ i) ^ 2 * (Real.log n + √(Real.pi * Real.log n) + 1) := by
  have hK : 0 ≤ σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2)) :=
    mul_nonneg (by positivity) (by linarith [Real.log_nonneg (le_add_of_nonneg_right
      (show 0 ≤ 2 * (σ2 : ℝ) / ε ^ 2 by positivity))])
  have hD : 0 ≤ 1 + 2 * σ2 / (μ j - ε - μ i) ^ 2 *
      (Real.log n + √(Real.pi * Real.log n) + 1) := by
    have := Real.log_natCast_nonneg n
    positivity
  have h_le := lintegral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit hσ h hε hij n
  rw [lintegral_pullCount_eq_ofReal_integral h.measurable_action, ← ENNReal.ofReal_one,
    ← ENNReal.ofReal_add zero_le_one hK, ← ENNReal.ofReal_add (by positivity) hD,
    ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal_iff (by positivity)] at h_le
  linarith

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **Asymptotic number of pulls of Gaussian Thompson sampling.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson
sampling with variance proxy `σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2`, for an arm
`a` with positive gap `Δ_a` and every `c > 2 σ² / Δ_a²`, the expected number of pulls of `a` during
the first `n` rounds is eventually at most `c log n`; that is,
`limsup_n E[T_a(n)] / log n ≤ 2 σ² / Δ_a²`. -/
theorem integral_pullCount_eventually_le [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {μ : α → ℝ} (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P) (a : α)
    (ha : 0 < gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a) {c : ℝ}
    (hc : 2 * σ2 / gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a ^ 2 < c) :
    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop, P[fun ω ↦ (pullCount A a n ω : ℝ)] ≤ c * Real.log n := by
  set ν := gaussianBandit μ σ2
  have hgap : gap ν a = μ (bestArm ν) - μ a := by
    rw [gap_eq_bestArm_sub, integral_id_gaussianBandit, integral_id_gaussianBandit]
  have hL : Filter.Tendsto (fun n : ℕ ↦ Real.log n / Real.log n) Filter.atTop (nhds 1) := by
    refine tendsto_const_nhds.congr' ?_
    filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_gt_atTop 1] with n hn
    exact (div_self (Real.log_pos (by exact_mod_cast hn)).ne').symm
  refine Real.eventually_le_mul_log_of_forall_le_add_mul_add_sqrt_add_one
    (L := fun n ↦ Real.log n) ha hL Real.pi_pos.le
    (fun ε hε ↦ ⟨2 + σ2 / ε ^ 2 * (8 + 2 * Real.log (1 + 2 * σ2 / ε ^ 2)), fun n ↦ ?_⟩) hc
  have h_le := integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit hσ h hε.1 (i := a) (j := bestArm ν)
    (by linarith [hε.2]) n
  rwa [show μ (bestArm ν) - ε - μ a = gap ν a - ε by rw [hgap]; ring] at h_le

omit [IsFiniteMeasure P] in
/-- **Logarithmic number of pulls of Gaussian Thompson sampling.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson
sampling with variance proxy `σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2`, let `n ≥ 3`
be a horizon and `a` an arm whose gap `Δ_a` satisfies `8 σ² ≤ n Δ_a²`. Then
`E[T_a(n)] ≤ 80 σ² log n / Δ_a² + 2`. This is the bound of
`integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit` for an optimal arm and the margin `ε = Δ_a / 2`. -/
theorem integral_pullCount_le_mul_log_div_gap_sq_add [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {μ : α → ℝ}
    (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P) {a : α}
    {n : ℕ} (hn : 3 ≤ n) (h_gap : 8 * σ2 ≤ n * gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a ^ 2) :
    P[fun ω ↦ (pullCount A a n ω : ℝ)] ≤
      80 * σ2 * Real.log n / gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a ^ 2 + 2 := by
  set ν := gaussianBandit μ σ2
  have hgap : gap ν a = μ (bestArm ν) - μ a := by
    rw [gap_eq_bestArm_sub, integral_id_gaussianBandit, integral_id_gaussianBandit]
  have hσ' : (0 : ℝ) < σ2 := NNReal.coe_pos.mpr (pos_iff_ne_zero.mpr hσ)
  have ha : 0 < gap ν a :=
    gap_pos_of_lt_mul_gap_sq le_rfl ((mul_pos (by norm_num) hσ').trans_le h_gap)
  set Δ := gap ν a
  set ℓ := Real.log n with hℓ_def
  have hℓ : 1 ≤ ℓ := Real.one_le_log_natCast_of_three_le hn
  have h_le := integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit hσ h (half_pos ha) (i := a)
    (j := bestArm ν) (by linarith) n
  -- With `ε = Δ / 2` and `c = σ² / Δ²`, the bound reads
  -- `2 + 4 c (8 + 2 log (1 + 8 c)) + 8 c (ℓ + √(π ℓ) + 1)`.
  set c := (σ2 : ℝ) / Δ ^ 2 with hc_def
  have hc : 0 ≤ c := by positivity
  have h_c4 : (σ2 : ℝ) / (Δ / 2) ^ 2 = 4 * c := by rw [hc_def]; field_simp; ring
  have h_c8 : 2 * (σ2 : ℝ) / (Δ / 2) ^ 2 = 8 * c := by rw [hc_def]; field_simp; ring
  rw [show μ (bestArm ν) - Δ / 2 - μ a = Δ / 2 by rw [hgap]; ring, h_c4, h_c8] at h_le
  rw [show 80 * (σ2 : ℝ) * ℓ / Δ ^ 2 = 80 * ℓ * c by rw [hc_def]; ring]
  -- `8 c ≤ n`, so `log (1 + 8 c) ≤ log (n ^ 2) = 2 ℓ`, and `√(π ℓ) ≤ 2 ℓ`.
  have h_8c : 8 * c ≤ n := by
    rw [hc_def, ← mul_div_assoc, div_le_iff₀ (by positivity)]
    exact h_gap
  have h_log : Real.log (1 + 8 * c) ≤ 2 * ℓ := by
    rw [hℓ_def, show 2 * Real.log n = Real.log ((n : ℝ) ^ 2) by rw [Real.log_pow]; norm_num]
    have hn' : (3 : ℝ) ≤ n := by exact_mod_cast hn
    exact Real.log_le_log (by positivity) (by nlinarith)
  have h_sqrt : √(Real.pi * ℓ) ≤ 2 * ℓ := by
    rw [Real.sqrt_le_left (by positivity)]
    nlinarith [Real.pi_le_four]
  -- `4 c (8 + 2 log (1 + 8 c)) + 8 c (ℓ + √(π ℓ) + 1) ≤ 40 c + 40 c ℓ ≤ 80 c ℓ`.
  linarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h_log hc, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h_sqrt hc,
    mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hℓ hc]

end GaussianTS

/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.3], upper bound of the asymptotic part.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson
sampling with variance proxy `σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2`, for every
`c > ∑_{a : Δ_a > 0} 2 σ² / Δ_a`, the expected regret at horizon `n` is eventually at most
`c log n`; that is, `limsup_n E[R_n] / log n ≤ ∑_{a : Δ_a > 0} 2 σ² / Δ_a`. -/
theorem gaussianTS_regret_eventually_le [StandardBorelSpace α] {σ2 : ℝ≥0} {Ω : Type*}
    {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {P : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {O : ℕ → Ω → Unit}
    {A : ℕ → Ω → α} {R : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} {μ : α → ℝ} (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P) {c : ℝ}
    (hc : ∑ a ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun a ↦ 0 < gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a),
      2 * σ2 / gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a < c) :
    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in Filter.atTop, P[regret (gaussianBandit μ σ2) A n] ≤ c * Real.log n := by
  refine integral_regret_eventually_le_of_forall_integral_pullCount_eventually_le
    h.measurable_action (.of_forall fun n ↦ Real.log_natCast_nonneg n)
    (fun a ↦ 2 * σ2 / gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a ^ 2)
    (fun a ha _ hc ↦ GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_eventually_le hσ h a ha hc) ?_
  refine (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a ha ↦ ?_).trans_lt hc
  field_simp [(Finset.mem_filter.mp ha).2.ne']

/-- **[LS, Theorem 36.3], minimax part.** In a run of Gaussian Thompson sampling with variance proxy
`σ² ≠ 0` against the Gaussian bandit `gaussianBandit μ σ2` with `k` arms, the expected regret at
horizon `n` is at most `18 √(σ² k n log n) + 2 ∑ a, Δ_a`.

[LS] states the additive term `∑ a, Δ_a`. The factor `2` here is the additive constant of the
bound `E[T_a(n)] ≤ 2 + ⋯` of `GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_le_of_gaussianBandit` on the expected
numbers of pulls, the sum of the constant `1` of [LS, Theorem 36.2] and of the term of the sample
size `0` in [LS, Exercise 36.6(b)]. -/
theorem gaussianTS_regret_le_sqrt [StandardBorelSpace α] {σ2 : ℝ≥0} {Ω : Type*}
    {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {P : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {O : ℕ → Ω → Unit}
    {A : ℕ → Ω → α} {R : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} {μ : α → ℝ} (hσ : σ2 ≠ 0)
    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A R (gaussianTS σ2) (Environment.bandit (gaussianBandit μ σ2)) P) (n : ℕ) :
    P[regret (gaussianBandit μ σ2) A n] ≤
      18 * √(σ2 * Fintype.card α * n * Real.log n) + 2 * ∑ a, gap (gaussianBandit μ σ2) a := by
  set ν := gaussianBandit μ σ2
  have h_sqrt : 0 ≤ 18 * √(σ2 * Fintype.card α * n * Real.log n) := by positivity
  rcases le_or_gt n 2 with hn | hn
  · -- For `n ≤ 2`, every arm is pulled at most twice.
    have h_le : P[regret ν A n] ≤ ∑ a, gap ν a * 2 :=
      integral_regret_le_of_forall_integral_pullCount_le h.measurable_action fun a _ ↦
        calc ∫ ω, (pullCount A a n ω : ℝ) ∂P ≤ ∫ _, (2 : ℝ) ∂P :=
              integral_mono_of_nonneg (.of_forall fun _ ↦ by positivity) (integrable_const _)
                (.of_forall fun ω ↦ by dsimp only; exact_mod_cast (pullCount_le a n ω).trans hn)
          _ = 2 := by simp
    rw [← Finset.sum_mul, mul_comm] at h_le
    linarith
  -- For `n ≥ 3`, apply the gap-free bound to the bound `80 σ² log n / Δ_a² + 2` on the pulls of
  -- the arms with `80 σ² log n k < n Δ_a²`, for which `n Δ_a² ≥ 80 σ² k log n ≥ 8 σ²`.
  set ℓ := Real.log n
  set k : ℝ := (Fintype.card α : ℝ)
  have hℓ : 1 ≤ ℓ := Real.one_le_log_natCast_of_three_le hn
  have hk : 1 ≤ k := Nat.one_le_cast.mpr Fintype.card_pos
  have h_kℓ : 8 * (σ2 : ℝ) ≤ 80 * σ2 * ℓ * k := by
    nlinarith [one_le_mul_of_one_le_of_one_le hℓ hk, σ2.coe_nonneg]
  have h_bound := integral_regret_le_two_mul_sqrt_add_of_forall_integral_pullCount_le
    h.measurable_action (C := 80 * σ2 * ℓ) (B := 2) (by positivity) zero_le_two fun a ha ↦
      GaussianTS.integral_pullCount_le_mul_log_div_gap_sq_add hσ h hn (h_kℓ.trans ha.le)
  -- `2 √(80 σ² log n k n) ≤ 18 √(σ² k n log n)`.
  have h_s : 2 * √(80 * σ2 * ℓ * k * n) ≤ 18 * √(σ2 * k * n * ℓ) := by
    rw [show 80 * (σ2 : ℝ) * ℓ * k * n = 80 * (σ2 * k * n * ℓ) by ring,
      Real.sqrt_mul (show (0 : ℝ) ≤ 80 by norm_num), ← mul_assoc]
    gcongr
    calc 2 * √80 ≤ 2 * √(9 ^ 2) := by gcongr; norm_num
      _ = 18 := by rw [Real.sqrt_sq (by norm_num)]; norm_num
  linarith

end Algorithm

